<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-Bertrand Aristide</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-Bertrand Aristide is a Haitian former Catholic priest and politician who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>'s first democratically elected president in 1990. A champion of the poor and critic of the Duvalier legacy, he was overthrown by a military coup in 1991 and restored by a US-led intervention in 1994. He was elected again in 2000, but amid an armed rebellion and foreign pressure he was removed and flown into exile in 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-bertrand-aristide.jpg" alt="Jean-Bertrand Aristide" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Communities, 1991 / EC - Audiovisual Service · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean-Bertrand_Aristide_-_1991_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
